# The news sources Whombat suggests (NEWS_SUGGESTIONS in packages/core/src/domain/news-suggestions.ts, written from
# this file by `node --import tsx scripts/weather-news/gen.ts`; docs/decisions/weather-news.md). Each row was fetched on
# the date in its last column and answered over https, without a redirect, within 1 MiB, with an RSS or Atom feed of
# recent items: `node --import tsx scripts/weather-news/check.ts --unchecked --write` reads the rows not checked yet as a
# Whombat does and notes what it found.
#
# Columns: id | country (ISO 3166-1) | regions (ISO 3166-2, the level-4 code: a province, state or Land; comma between
# several) | areas (ISO 3166-2 level 6, where the region is too large: a Belgian province) | where (the region's or
# area's own name, “Noord-Brabant”; only for those) | language | topic (tech, business, sport, science or culture;
# empty: all the news) | name | feed | checked.
#
# A row without regions or areas is for the whole country. Per country: its outlets' “all news” feeds first, then their
# topic feeds (not every section), then the regional ones. Only https feeds, and none whose terms rule out a paid
# product (Yle) or a feed made for personal readers only (Google News); when a site's terms are unclear, leave it out.
# Keep a row's id once it is in: a burrow keeps the ids it turned on.
